# Shell scripts must stay LF regardless of core.autocrlf, or bash on Windows
# fails on the trailing carriage return.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Dependency manifests must stay UTF-8 text with LF, or PowerShell redirection
# writes UTF-16 and git stores them as binary with no reviewable diff.
requirements*.txt text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts: keep LF in the repo so core.autocrlf does not leave them
# permanently "modified", which blocks rebase with "you have unstaged changes".
# They carry a UTF-8 BOM, which Windows PowerShell 5.1 needs to parse them.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
